   "date": "2014-02-27T12:14:18Z",
   "subject": "Re: No layer with geom_tile( )",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hi, since you want your fill as part of your canvas, you should declare it within the aesthetics:<div><br></div><div><div>library(ggplot2)</div><div>data &lt;- read.csv(&quot;sample.csv&quot;)</div></div><div><div>p1 &lt;- ggplot(data, aes(x,y, fill=value))</div><div>p1 + geom_tile()</div><div><br></div><div>or:</div><div>p1 &lt;- p1 + geom_tile()</div><div>p1</div><div><br></div><div>if you really wanted to.</div><div><br></div><div>Cheers,</div><div><br></div><div>Richard</div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
